		"lang": "en",
		"notes": [
			{
				"category": "summary",
				"text": "An updated elinks package that corrects a security vulnerability is now\navailable for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 4.\n\nThis update has been rated as having critical security impact by the Red\nHat Security Response Team.",
				"title": "Topic"
			},
			{
				"category": "general",
				"text": "Elinks is a text mode Web browser used from the command line that supports\nrendering modern web pages.\n\nAn arbitrary file access flaw was found in the Elinks SMB protocol handler.\nA malicious web page could have caused Elinks to read or write files with\nthe permissions of the user running Elinks. (CVE-2006-5925)\n\nAll users of Elinks are advised to upgrade to this updated package, which\nresolves this issue by removing support for the SMB protocol from Elinks.\n\nNote: this issue did not affect the Elinks package shipped with Red Hat\nEnterprise Linux 3, or the Links package shipped with Red Hat Enterprise\nLinux 2.1.",
				"title": "Details"
			},
			{
				"category": "legal_disclaimer",
				"text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to Red Hat Inc. and provide a link to the original.",
				"title": "Terms of Use"
			}
		],
